{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Truly my bone and my flesh are you.</b> By strict justice I should have kept you away from me, just as you kept away from your other relatives, since you deceived your brother twice. But: my bone and my flesh are you — and I shall not keep you away." "<b>And he stayed with him a month of days.</b> The Torah teaches proper conduct: how long must a person attend to his relatives? Another interpretation: Lavan heard what Jacob did to Esau and was afraid to hire him until he tested him to see what his way of dealing was." "<b>A month of days.</b> A full month of days."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:35.794240859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}